'[{"week":1,"title":"Assessment Design Fundamentals","tasks":["Study Bloom''s Taxonomy for question design","Learn the difference between knowledge, application, and analysis questions","Study what makes a good MCQ (plausible distractors, clear stems)","Analyze 10 UPSC papers from an assessment quality perspective"]},{"week":2,"title":"Item Writing Practice","tasks":["Write 50 high-quality MCQs for one GS paper","Write 10 descriptive questions with marking schemes","Review your questions against assessment quality standards","Get feedback from UPSC coaching faculty"]},{"week":3,"title":"Target Organizations","tasks":["Apply to NTA (National Testing Agency) for content roles","Apply to UPSC Commission support organizations","Apply to State PSC technical units","Apply to EdTech platforms for assessment roles"]},{"week":4,"title":"EdTech Assessment Market","tasks":["Apply to Unacademy, PW, Byju''s assessment teams","Apply to Testbook and Adda247 question bank teams","Apply to Career Launcher for assessment design","These platforms need thousands of quality questions"]},{"week":5,"title":"Psychometrics Basics","tasks":["Study Item Difficulty and Item Discrimination concepts","Learn Classical Test Theory basics","Practice item analysis with sample data","Study reliability and validity in assessment"]},{"week":6,"title":"Descriptive Assessment","tasks":["Design an essay assessment rubric","Create an evaluator training guide","Practice scoring essays against rubric","Study UPSC Mains descriptive assessment design"]},{"week":7,"title":"Digital Assessment","tasks":["Learn about Computer Adaptive Testing (CAT)","Study online proctoring technology","Understand LMS-based assessment delivery","Explore Moodle quiz design"]},{"week":8,"title":"Freelance Assessment Work","tasks":["Register on platforms offering assessment freelancing","Set rate: ₹100-500 per question depending on complexity","Build quality portfolio of 500 questions","Apply to international assessment companies with India presence"]},{"week":9,"title":"Government Examination Bodies","tasks":["Research UPSC, SSC, IBPS content development processes","Understand how state PSC question papers are developed","Apply for empanelment as subject matter expert","Build relationships with examination officials"]},{"week":10,"title":"International Orgs","tasks":["Research British Council, IDP, ETS India assessment opportunities","Cambridge Assessment International qualifications need paper setters","Apply as Associate Paper Setter","International rates are significantly higher"]},{"week":11,"title":"Build Expertise","tasks":["Specialize in 2-3 subjects where you have deepest knowledge","Build reputation as domain specialist","Write on assessment quality issues for EdTech publications","Build a public portfolio"]},{"week":12,"title":"Launch","tasks":["Build a sustainable freelance assessment income","Set target: 500 questions/month at ₹200 average = ₹1 lakh/month","Plan full-time role at an examination body","Set long-term goals in assessment industry"]}]',
'₹3,000-10,000 (minimal investment needed)',
'Apply to NTA, state PSC technical units, and EdTech platforms (Testbook, PW, Byju''s) directly. Also register on freelancing platforms for assessment work. State public service commission examiners are often contracted as subject matter experts.',
'[{"title":"Educational Testing Service","url":"https://www.youtube.com/@ETSEducation","channel":"ETS"},{"title":"National Testing Agency India","url":"https://www.youtube.com/@NTAIndia","channel":"NTA"}]',
